# SHA-256 checksums for the vendored third-party JavaScript.
#
# Purpose: pin the exact bytes of the opaque minified libraries so any change to them is visible
# in review. This records integrity, not upstream provenance — to prove these match the published
# npm releases byte-for-byte, run the `npm pack` + hash comparison documented in the security
# review (FINDINGS.md, "Bundled JS provenance").
#
# Verify (from this directory):
#   sha256sum -c CHECKSUMS.sha256
# On Windows PowerShell:
#   Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 cytoscape.min.js,dagre.min.js,cytoscape-dagre.js
#
# Claimed upstream versions: cytoscape.js 3.30.4, dagre 0.8.5, cytoscape-dagre 2.x.
# SECURITY NOTE: dagre 0.8.5 is unmaintained and bundles an old lodash with known
# prototype-pollution CVEs — see FINDINGS.md. renderGraph() drops reserved node ids as a
# stopgap; the durable fix is migrating to @dagrejs/dagre 1.x.

50fdaaf3f6f45774c7368f2ffb927246423679efc364d0ebe47cebcfa3eed1e8  cytoscape.min.js
baed8315af2db75edef6d0fec8e08b7a28508e62d469b65e77c93b27e38bff67  dagre.min.js
57fa1d16bcdb9a66792a597a2b80f88c0bd0daefcef595dd5a8821cf88262aea  cytoscape-dagre.js
